From 668758ff58acadf99e7be731939daeda6d2f1443 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:04:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tangent operator applied without assembly (MatrixFree)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New value MatrixFree of the TangentOperatorComputation parameter (and of
the MFEM_MGIS_TANGENT_OPERATOR_COMPUTATION environment variable): the
tangent operator returned by GetGradient is applied without assembly,
by kernels (MatrixFreeTangentOperator, y = Pᵀ (Σ Bᵀ K B w det J) P x,
whose diagonal is computed by kernels by AssembleDiagonal), the
essential degrees of freedom being constrained by
mfem::ConstrainedOperator. The non linear form must only contain the
integrator of mfem-mgis (otherwise, an exception is thrown). The
prediction uses the operator assembled by kernels.

The linear solver must not require a matrix: the OperatorJacobiSmoother
preconditioner (option Damping) is added to the linear solvers of MFEM,
its diagonal being computed by AssembleDiagonal, or by GetDiag for a
sparse matrix (MFEM 4.10 does not implement AssembleDiagonal for
mfem::SparseMatrix).

BatchIntegrationTest: computations with the tangent operator applied
without assembly, the conjugate gradient of MFEM and the Jacobi
preconditioner, compared to the integration point by point (small and
finite strain, orthotropic, plane strain, two materials, prediction,
behaviours of the generic-parallel interface, on the debug device, on
the GPU and on two processes).
